// Pull request: #6435 Add Linux rule: Potential Command Execution Via Tar Checkpoint Or To-Command
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6435
// Pull request author: defamp
// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential Command Execution Via Tar Checkpoint Or To-Command
// Sigma ID: 06b92d88-4846-4b13-bde5-7119a5118aef
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Defa Mulya Pratama
// Date: 2026-10-07 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059
// Description: Detects the use of the "tar" utility with the "--checkpoint-action" or "--to-command" options.
//   These options allow "tar" to execute arbitrary commands and are abused for privilege escalation
//   (e.g. via "sudo tar"), to break out of restricted environments, or through tar wildcard
//   injection where crafted file names are expanded by the shell and interpreted by "tar" as
//   command-line options.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely. The "--checkpoint-action" and "--to-command" options are rarely used in legitimate automation and should be investigated.
// References:
//   - https://gtfobins.github.io/gtfobins/tar/
//   - https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/security/current/linux-restricted-shell-breakout-via-linux-binary-s.html
//   - https://www.exploit-db.com/papers/33930
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/0bb311b78aad23c531958c2e467936c8a85a1ddd/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_tar_command_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/tar" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "--checkpoint-action" or ProcessCommandLine contains "--to-command")
